        "image": "shopify://shop_images/av-home-story.jpg",
        "label": "The house",
        "text": "<p>Every piece begins as a length of silk cotton, its weft spun by hand and woven on a pit loom in Tamil Nadu. Kamalam Moorthy, who designs the cloth and runs its production, draws each motif from the temples, the forests and the stories told about them.</p><p>The embroidery is aari work in metallic thread, done by hand by our senior artisan. A veshti spends about six weeks between the loom and the embroidery frame before it is finished, which is why there are only a few of each.</p>",
